---
import Layout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectHero from '../../components/features/projects/ProjectHero.astro';
import AchievementCard from '../../components/common/AchievementCard.astro';
import MetricsTable from '../../components/common/MetricsTable.astro';
import ProjectDetailSection from '../../components/features/projects/ProjectDetailSection.astro';
import ProjectTags from '../../components/features/projects/ProjectTags.astro';

const title = 'OpenAI-Powered Documentation Quality Feedback System';
const description = 'Developed an end-to-end solution using the OpenAI API to ingest de-identified patient notes and generate actionable feedback—ensuring technicians and providers produce documentation that meets Blue Cross Blue Shield audit standards.';
const date = new Date('2023-11-01T00:00:00.000Z');
const tags = ['OpenAI', 'Natural Language Processing', 'Healthcare IT', 'Compliance', 'Blue Cross Blue Shield', 'Documentation Quality', 'Python'];
const image = '/assets/images/default-project.png';
const canonicalUrl = 'https://blakeoxford.com/projects/LLM-note-coaching/';

const metrics = [
  {
    metric: 'Audit Exceptions',
    result: '50% reduction',
    timeline: 'Post-implementation'
  },
  {
    metric: 'Compliance Review Time',
    result: '20+ hours/week saved',
    timeline: 'Automated processing'
  },
  {
    metric: 'Teams Message Engagement',
    result: '+40% after tone adjustment',
    timeline: 'Balanced feedback approach'
  },
  {
    metric: 'Revision Turnaround',
    result: '-30% improvement',
    timeline: 'Strengths-focused feedback'
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  image={image}
  url={canonicalUrl}
  wide={true}
>
  <ProjectHero 
    title={title}
    description={description}
    date={date}
    image={image}
  />

  <article class="relative isolate overflow-hidden bg-gradient-to-b from-surface-subtle via-background to-background py-24">
    <div
      class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 bg-grid-overlay/30 [background-size:200px_200px]"
      aria-hidden="true"
    ></div>
    <div class="layout-shell-wide relative flex flex-col gap-14">
      <ProjectDetailSection title="Project introduction" eyebrow="🏥 Background">
        <div class="space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-foreground/78 dark:text-foreground-light/82">
          <p>
            Hourly technicians—many fresh out of high school—were expected to craft medical documentation that satisfied payers, providers, and regulators. We had dashboards for missing signatures and CPT mismatches, but nothing evaluated whether the story in the note actually conveyed medical necessity.
          </p>
          <p>
            Shadowing the floor and running quick interviews exposed the missing ingredient: coaching. Staff knew <em>when</em> notes failed audits but not <em>why</em>. The solution had to scale empathy, not just enforcement.
          </p>
        </div>
      </ProjectDetailSection>

      <ProjectDetailSection title="Discovery insights" eyebrow="🔎 Finding the real pain" layout="surface">
        <ul class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-foreground/78 dark:text-foreground-light/82">
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="mt-1 inline-flex h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
            <span>Days shadowing frontline staff revealed note-writing friction points in real time.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="mt-1 inline-flex h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
            <span>Lightning interviews surfaced a universal answer to “What’s hardest about notes?”—no feedback on narrative quality.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="mt-1 inline-flex h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
            <span>Opportunity reframed: wield an LLM not as a grader, but as a mentor that teaches storytelling and compliance.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </ProjectDetailSection>

      <ProjectDetailSection title="Technical highlights" eyebrow="🧠 Architecture">
        <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-1">
          <AchievementCard 
            title="Secure ETL pipeline"
            achievements={[
              'Python + SQL Server pipeline de-identified notes (names, dates, identifiers) under HIPAA guardrails before leaving the data center.'
            ]}
          />
          <AchievementCard 
            title="Prompt engineering for BCBS"
            achievements={[
              'Collaborated with auditors and BCBAs to craft GPT-4 prompts assessing medical necessity, CPT justification, narrative clarity, and treatment rationale.'
            ]}
          />
          <AchievementCard 
            title="Role-based feedback"
            achievements={[
              'Technicians received structural coaching while providers got guidance on clinical rationale, goal alignment, and regulatory guardrails.'
            ]}
          />
          <AchievementCard 
            title="Power BI intelligence"
            achievements={[
              'Dashboards visualized audit readiness by author, location, and time to focus coaching energy where it mattered most.'
            ]}
          />
          <AchievementCard 
            title="Azure automation"
            achievements={[
              'Nightly Azure Functions batches triggered Microsoft Graph notifications and risk alerts when systemic issues emerged.'
            ]}
          />
        </div>
      </ProjectDetailSection>

      <ProjectDetailSection title="Design sprints" eyebrow="🌀 Iteration cadence" layout="surface">
        <div class="space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-foreground/78 dark:text-foreground-light/82">
          <p>Three rapid prompt-tuning loops in a single week kept humans in the center of the experience:</p>
          <ol class="space-y-4 pl-6 text-foreground/80 marker:text-foreground/45">
            <li><strong>Draft prompt:</strong> test against sample notes and capture raw reactions.</li>
            <li><strong>Tone adjust:</strong> balance critique with encouragement; measure “feedback acknowledged” rates.</li>
            <li><strong>Final prompt:</strong> pilot with the field and monitor adoption, compliance metrics, and morale.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>This cadence ensured the LLM sounded supportive, not punitive.</p>
        </div>
      </ProjectDetailSection>

      <ProjectDetailSection title="Data-driven refinement" eyebrow="📈 What we measured">
        <ul class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-foreground/78 dark:text-foreground-light/82">
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="mt-1 inline-flex h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
            <span><strong>Teams message opens</strong> climbed 40% after softening tone and spotlighting wins.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="mt-1 inline-flex h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
            <span><strong>Revision turnaround</strong> improved 30% when feedback balanced strengths with specific corrections.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </ProjectDetailSection>

      <ProjectDetailSection title="Audit enforcer → coaching engine" eyebrow="🔄 Transformation" layout="surface">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[2rem] ring-1 ring-border/25">
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left text-sm text-foreground/82 dark:text-foreground-light/80">
              <thead class="bg-surface-subtle/80 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-foreground/70 dark:bg-surface-dark-subtle">
                <tr>
                  <th class="px-6 py-4">🔍 Old: Audit enforcer</th>
                  <th class="px-6 py-4">🌱 New: Skill developer</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-border/20">
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Flagged only what was missing</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Highlighted strengths <em>and</em> gaps</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="bg-background/70">
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Delivered blunt, clinical feedback</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Delivered empathetic, balanced feedback</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Focused on passing audits</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Focused on building documentation skill</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="bg-background/70">
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Seen as punitive by technicians</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Seen as a collaborative mentor</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Treated the model like a grader</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Treated the model like a coach</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="bg-background/70">
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Designed for outcomes</td>
                  <td class="px-6 py-4">Designed for <em>growth</em></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </ProjectDetailSection>

      <ProjectDetailSection title="Human impact" eyebrow="🤝 Collaboration">
        <div class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-foreground/78 dark:text-foreground-light/82">
          <p>
            “It’s really helpful to see <strong>why</strong> good notes matter.” Technicians felt encouraged rather than judged, and providers noticed the AI surfaced subtleties they sometimes missed—proving that the real power is human + AI teamwork.
          </p>
        </div>
      </ProjectDetailSection>

      <ProjectDetailSection title="Impact & results" eyebrow="📊 Outcomes" layout="surface">
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <MetricsTable metrics={metrics} />
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground/78 dark:text-foreground-light/82 md:text-base">
            <li class="flex gap-4">
              <span class="mt-1 inline-flex h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
              <span>Technician confidence and skill growth accelerated with every revision cycle.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-4">
              <span class="mt-1 inline-flex h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
              <span>Architecture remains payer-agnostic, ready to adapt for Aetna, UnitedHealthcare, and future audit frameworks.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </ProjectDetailSection>

      <ProjectDetailSection title="Novelty & transferability" eyebrow="🧬 Pattern reuse">
        <div class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-foreground/78 dark:text-foreground-light/82">
          <p>
            The recipe scales: identify a manual compliance pain point, reframe it as a coaching challenge, and pair domain experts with an LLM co-pilot. The same pattern could uplift imaging protocols, pharmacy reviews, discharge summaries—anywhere passive checks stall learning.
          </p>
        </div>
      </ProjectDetailSection>

      <ProjectDetailSection title="Reflection" eyebrow="🗒️ Takeaway" layout="surface">
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-foreground/78 dark:text-foreground-light/82">
          Combining empathy, rapid iteration, and LLM expertise turned a compliance complaint into a learning engine. When technology is aligned with human needs, it doesn’t just prevent mistakes—it raises the bar for everyone involved.
        </p>
      </ProjectDetailSection>
    </div>
  </article>

  <ProjectTags tags={tags} />
</Layout> 